<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for Developer ID (release) signing only.

  These are inert without the hardened runtime, so macos-sign-app.sh applies
  this file exclusively on the Developer ID path. Under the hardened runtime
  the camera and microphone are denied outright unless claimed here. The
  Info.plist usage descriptions control the wording of the consent prompt, not
  whether the process is permitted to ask at all.

  Note for editors: AMFI parses this file at signing time with a stricter XML
  reader than plutil. A doubled hyphen anywhere inside this comment is invalid
  XML and makes codesign fail with "AMFIUnserializeXML: syntax error", even
  though "plutil -lint" reports the file as OK.

  Deliberately absent:

  com.apple.security.app-sandbox. Toki ships outside the App Store, where
  sandboxing is not required, and the sandbox would sever screen capture and
  the accessibility APIs that locate on-screen targets.

  com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit. MediaPipe's WebAssembly runs inside
  WKWebView's out-of-process WebContent process, which carries Apple's own
  entitlements. Toki's own process never JITs.

  com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation. The bundle links no
  third-party dylibs or frameworks; the only Mach-O image is the main binary.

  Every entitlement widens the attack surface the hardened runtime exists to
  narrow. Add one only when a reproducible failure demands it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
